-- | OpenZeppelin Pausable - the interface for an emergency-stop switch on a
-- Daml template.
--
-- The implementing template holds a `paused` flag and implements `Pausable`.
-- The guards, the flips, and the failure statuses live in the separate
-- `openzeppelin-pausable-v1` package, module `OpenZeppelin.PausableV1`, so
-- that a fix to them ships without touching this frozen interface.
--
-- The flag is a field of the contract being exercised, so a guard reads it
-- with no extra fetch, no extra disclosure, and no extra authority.
--
-- The consumer decides who may pause. Authorization lives in the controller
-- and body of the consumer's flip choice, so any model fits: a single party,
-- a role grant, an M-of-N approval, or a timelock.
--
-- The switch is per contract and applies to new transactions: a gated choice
-- refuses to start while the flag is set.
module OpenZeppelin.Api.PausableV1 where

-- | Whether an implementing contract is currently paused.
data PausableView = PausableView with
    paused : Bool
      -- ^ Whether the contract is currently paused.
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | The switch. Implement it on any template that holds a pause flag.
interface Pausable where
  viewtype PausableView

  setPaused : Bool -> Pausable
    -- ^ Return this template's own value with the flag set and every other
    --   field unchanged:
    --
    --   ```
    --   setPaused b = toInterface (this with paused = b)
    --   ```
    --
    --   `pause` and `unpause` in `OpenZeppelin.PausableV1` call this method
    --   and verify the result. Call those from choice bodies instead of
    --   `setPaused` directly.
